            "spacing": "Small"
          },
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "text": "Three items stayed hot every day the board ran: Defense Distributed v. Blanche peaked at 91 after a judge held ATF's frame-and-receiver rule unconstitutional — as-applied to the parties, not nationwide. DOJ's final rights-restoration rule held an 85 average with its text still unread from primary source.",
            "wrap": true,
            "spacing": "Small"
